    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 510 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1863A\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 510 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of a hotel and motel tax in the town of Wood-\nbury, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the town of Woodbury's authority to impose a hotel and motel\ntax.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 2 of chapter 510 of the laws of 2016, to\nextend the expiration date of the existing hotel and motel tax in the\ntown of Woodbury.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the town of Woodbury to extend the expira-\ntion date of the currently existing hotel and motel tax. The rate of\nsuch tax shall not exceed 5% of the per diem rental rate for each room.\nPursuant to the Municipal Home Rule Law, a town may adopt local laws\nthat relate to the levy and administration of local taxes if authorized\nby the State legislature. The town of Woodbury has requested special\nlegislation that will enable them to extend their ability to collect a\nhotel and motel tax in an effort to raise additional revenue for the\ntown.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
